# Chapter 11, part 2: print and preview jobs, the Printer, the Document Manager
# and the Viewer.
.h2 Print and preview jobs [msg-job]
.ix Messages, Print
.ix Messages, Preview
.ix Print messages
.ix Preview messages
.ix Print job messages
These messages are shown when a PDF is made and sent to a queue, and when a
preview is made.  Two commands show them: the Print panel of the Editor
(Draft and Final) and its Preview.  The tables say where.  {X:print-messages} describes the
same messages in the context of those commands.
.h3 Values that are refused [msg-job-check]
.ix Refused values, print
.ix Copies, message
.ix Printer queue, message
A value is refused before anything is made.  In the Print panel the message is
in a box titled Marker ({n:msg-ed-panels}) and the panel stays open.
.table 28 32
Message | Meaning and what to do
A page must be a number from 1 to 99999 | Print from Page or to Page is not a
 | whole number in that range.  Type digits.
A page range needs a printer: name one in Printer | A page range, and the
 | printer is File only or PDF viewer. A page range can be printed only to a
 | queue.  With PDF viewer the message ends with the words "(the program that
 | opens the PDF has its own print dialog)".  The same
 | message begins with another phrase when the fault is another one:
 | {c:More than one copy}, {c:Double sided} or {c:Sort output pages}.  Name a queue, or
 | take the default values.
Cannot find section number NAME | Print from Section or to Section names a
 | section that the document does not have.  Look at the numbers on the screen.
Cannot find the directory DIR | The directory of Output File does not exist.
Cannot write in the directory DIR | The directory of Output File exists and
 | cannot be written.
Contents Levels is a number from 1 to 99 | Table of Contents? is Yes and
 | Contents Levels is not a whole number from 1 to 99.
Copies must be a number from 1 to 99 | Copies is not a whole number in that
 | range.
NAME is a directory | Output File names a directory.  Add a file name.
"NAME" is not the name of a printer queue | The text typed as the printer
 | cannot be a queue: it begins with a minus, contains a space or one of /
 | # \ ' " , or is 128 letters or longer.  Press {k:F2} in the field for the
 | queues that the system lists ({n:print-sending}).
No output file given | Output File is empty.
Only a structured document has sections | Print from Section in an
 | unstructured document.
The first page is after the last page | Print from Page is greater than to
 | Page.
The first section is after the last | The sections named are in the wrong
 | order.
The PDF cannot replace the document | Output File is the path of the document.
There is no current section | Print Current Section Only? (box titled Print)
 | and the cursor is in no section.
.end
.h3 The run and its end [msg-job-run]
.ix Wrote, message
.ix lp failed
.ix Print failed
.ix Print cancelled
.ix Cancelled while sending
.ix Print stopped by a signal
.ix LaTeX failed
.ix Print needs
.ix lp was not found
These are the texts that a print makes when it has run.  A good print without
a queue ends with one line; a failure or a good print with lp shows a box
(titled Print).  The Document
Manager shows the first line of a good print on its footer ({n:msg-docmgr}).
.table 30 30
Message | Meaning and what to do
Cancelled while sending to QUEUE. The PDF PATH was made; the print job may or
 may not have been queued. | {k:Esc} was pressed while lp ran.  Look at the
 | queue (the print system's own command) before printing again.
Cannot make a temporary directory: REASON | The working directory of the job
 | cannot be made.  Free space or rights in the directory that {c:TMPDIR}
 | names.
Cannot start <Printer>: REASON | The Printer could not be started: no memory
 | or no process.
Cannot write in DIR | The working directory of the job cannot be written.
Cannot write the PDF: REASON | The PDF is made but cannot be put at its place:
 | the directory is full or protected.
LaTeX failed: TEXT1 TEXT2 | LaTeX stopped. TEXT1 is the first error line of
 | the log (it begins with an exclamation mark) and TEXT2 the line after.
 | Nothing is written.  See {x:msg-other-latex}.
lp failed (status N): TEXT  Nothing was sent and no PDF was kept: choose File
 only to keep one. | lp ended with an error and the PDF of a print to a queue
 | was deleted.
lp failed (status N): TEXT The PDF PATH was made. | lp ended with an error and
 | TEXT is its own message (for example the queue does not exist).  The PDF is
 | kept and can be printed with another command.
Print cancelled | {k:Esc} was pressed during the typesetting; nothing is sent
 | and no PDF is written.  The Document Manager shows it on its footer when it
 | stops the job.
Print failed (<Printer> ended with status N) | The Printer failed without a
 | message of its own.
Print failed: TEXT | The Printer wrote TEXT as its message ({n:msg-printer}).
PRINT FAILED: Wrote PATH (N pages).  E errors and W warnings. | The PDF is made
 | and not sent, and the document has errors: the print FAILED and every page
 | has the banner and the marks ({n:print-failed}).
Print needs <Printer>: it was not found next to <Editor> or in the system
 directories. | The
 | program that makes the PDF is not installed.
Print needs LaTeX: pdflatex was not found in FOLDERS. See README.txt for the
 packages. | The prerequisites are not met: install the LaTeX packages.
Print stopped by a signal | The Editor got SIGINT, SIGTERM or SIGHUP during
 | the job.  The working files are removed.
Sent to QUEUE: N pages, C copies, SIDES.  No PDF was kept | A print to a queue:
 | lp took the pages; the PDF that was made for it is deleted.
The PDF PATH was made but lp could not be started. | lp exists and cannot run.
The PDF PATH was made but lp did not answer within a minute. | lp was stopped
 | after 60 seconds.  The PDF is kept.
The PDF PATH was made but was not sent. TEXT | The page range or the queue was
 | refused after the PDF was made. TEXT is one of: {c:No printer is named},
 | {c:The PDF must be given with its full path},
 | {c:The document has only N pages, so it has no page N} (the first page is past the end), or one of the
 | refusals of {x:msg-job-check}.
The printer NAME is not in the list of the system any more: File only is shown |
 | The Print panel kept NAME from the last print and the system does not report
 | it now.  The panel opens with File only.
Wrote PATH | The PDF is made.  The page count was not known.
Wrote PATH and sent it to QUEUE (ANSWER) | The same when the page count was
 | not known.
Wrote PATH but lp was not found, so it was not sent to QUEUE. Install
 cups-client. | The PDF is made; the print command is not
 | installed.
Wrote PATH (N pages) | The PDF is made and not sent. {c:1 page} for one.
Wrote PATH (N pages) and opened it to print | PDF viewer: the PDF is made
 | and a program that shows PDF files was started.
Wrote PATH (N pages) and sent it to QUEUE (ANSWER) | lp took the PDF. ANSWER
 | is the answer of lp, such as {c:request id is laser-17 (1 file(s))}, or
 | {c:no answer from lp}.
Wrote PATH (N pages) but no PDF viewer was found: set one in Setup: it is saved
 | PDF viewer, and no such program or no display, or the setting pdf_viewer
 | names a word processor.  The PDF is kept.
Wrote PATH (N pages) but the program of the setting pdf_viewer was not found:
 it is saved | The setting names a program that is not there.
Wrote PATH (N pages) but the program that opens it could not be started: it is
 saved | The program could not be run.
.end
The Print panel has one more text, a line {c:Print Status} that shows only when
 lp is
not installed: {c:lp not found: only the PDF is made}.  It is a notice: the
 panel is
accepted, and a print makes the PDF but cannot send it.
.h3 The texts of the progress box [msg-job-progress]
.ix Progress box
.ix Running LaTeX
While a print or a preview runs the Editor shows a box with a bar.  Its texts
 are
not errors.
.table 28 32
Text | When
Another pass, for the references. | The second or third run of LaTeX, which is
 | made because page references or a table of contents moved.
Close the viewer to return. | The Viewer is open (Preview).
Page N of about M | LaTeX is on page N; M is an estimate. {c:Page N of M} when
 | it is sure.
Running LaTeX (pass N) | LaTeX runs; N is the number of the pass.
Sending to the printer | lp is running. {k:Esc} stops lp (the hint in the box
 | says {c:Esc stops lp}).
Writing | The document is being prepared for typesetting.
.end
.h3 Preview [msg-job-preview]
.ix Preview, failure
.ix Viewer, not found
.ix X display, Preview
The three messages that begin with {c:Preview needs} are boxes titled Preview;
 the
others are on the message line.
.table 30 30
Message | Meaning and what to do
LaTeX failed: TEXT1 TEXT2 | LaTeX stopped and no preview was made.  See
 | {x:msg-other-latex}.
Preview cancelled | {k:Esc} while the preview was made.
Preview: cannot make a temporary directory: REASON | As for a print.
Preview: cannot run the viewer PATH | The Viewer exists and cannot run.
Preview: cannot start <Printer>: REASON | As for a print.
Preview: cannot write in DIR | The working directory cannot be written.
Preview done | The Viewer was closed after a good preview.
Preview done: PRINT FAILED, N print errors (Ctrl-F8 finds the next) | The
 | Viewer was closed after a preview that had errors; its pages and the
 | Viewer's red area said PRINT FAILED ({n:print-failed}).
Preview done; the viewer could not show N things: TEXT | The Viewer left
 | something out of the pages (TEXT names the first); the preview is
 | otherwise good.  When the run has a log the line ends with "; details in
 | the log of the run" ({n:appcfg-log}).
Preview failed (<Printer> ended with status N) | The Printer failed without a
 | message.
Preview failed: TEXT | The Printer wrote TEXT as its message.
Preview needs <Printer>: it was not found next to <Editor> or in the system
 directories. | The
 | program that typesets is not installed.
Preview needs an X display: DISPLAY is not set.  Run <Editor> under X, or use
 the X11 version. | The Viewer opens a window.  There is no display.
Preview needs the viewer <Viewer>: it was not found next to <Editor> or in
 the system directories. | The Viewer is not installed.  Install the Viewer.
Preview shown in spite of errors of LaTeX: TEXT1 TEXT2 | The preview has
 | pages, but LaTeX met an error: some part of the text may be missing or
 | wrong.  Read TEXT1.
Preview: the viewer failed: TEXT | The Viewer ended with an error; TEXT is
 | the reason.  When the run has a log the line ends with "; details in the
 | log of the run" ({n:appcfg-log}).
.end
.h2 The Printer [msg-printer]
.ix Messages, Printer
.ix Printer, error output
.ix Printer, messages
The Editor shows the messages of the Printer after {c:Print failed: } or
{c:Preview failed: } ({n:msg-job}).  The tables write each with the prefix
{c:<Printer>: }.
.table 32 28
Message | Meaning and what to do
<Printer>: cannot make a temporary directory: REASON | The working directory
 | cannot be made.
<Printer>: cannot write in DIR | The working directory cannot be written.
 |
<Printer>: cannot write PATH | The PDF, the pages of a Preview or the TeX
 | source cannot be written; or a picture cannot be copied next to them.
<Printer>: FILE: dvipdfmx failed | The PDF could not be made from the DVI
 | file.
<Printer>: FILE: ENGINE did not run (is it installed? sudo apt install
 texlive-latex-recommended texlive-latex-extra texlive-extra-utils lmodern)
 | The program ENGINE (pdflatex or latex) did not run.  Install the packages
 | named.
<Printer>: FILE: ENGINE failed, no error line in LOGFILE | The engine failed
 | and the log has no line that begins with an exclamation mark.  Read the log,
 | kept with the option that keeps the files.
<Printer>: FILE: REASON | FILE could not be loaded.  REASON is one of the
 | messages about a file that are listed in {x:msg-ed-file}: the file cannot
 | be opened or read, is damaged, is not a document of this software, or has
 | a version that is not read.
<Printer>: FILE: ! TEXT | LaTeX stopped at the first error and no PDF was
 | made: the text is the first error line of the log.  See
 | {x:msg-other-latex}.
<Printer>: files kept in DIR | A notice with the option that keeps the files:
 | the directory holds the TeX source and the log.
<Printer>: PATH exists and differs: the picture is not copied | The pictures
 | of a Preview are copied next to its pages, and a different file of the same
 | name is there. A notice; the other file is not changed.
{c:<Printer>: warning: PLACE: No font has the character U+XXXX; it is printed as [U+XXXX]. [char-missing]} | A
 | character of the document has no letter in the font.  A warning: the PDF is
 | made, and the character is printed as the bracketed number.  XXXX is the
 | number of the character in Unicode.  Choose another font ({n:print-fonts}) or
 | delete the character.  The same text is in the Error Log ({n:msg-errlog}).
.end
.h2 The Document Manager [msg-docmgr]
.ix Messages, Document Manager
.ix Document Manager, messages
.ix Footer messages
The Document Manager shows a message on its footer line (the text stays until
 the
next key and replaces the hint), in a box that ends with a key, or on the error
output.  The same messages are in {n:str} with their panels.
.h3 The footer [msg-docmgr-footer]
.ix Footer, Document Manager
.table 30 30
Text | Meaning and what to do
Cannot find directory DIR | The Working Directory of a panel does not exist.
Enter a document name | The field Document Name is empty.
Installation cancelled | TeX Font Association, Install Now: {k:Esc} stopped the
 | download ({n:msg-other-font}).
Settings saved to PATH | Setup was accepted and written.
.end
.h3 Boxes [msg-docmgr-boxes]
.ix Boxes, Document Manager
.table 20 18 22
Title: text | Where | Meaning and what to do
Edit / Preview / Print Document: Cannot run the editor: PATH | Edit / Preview /
 | Print Document | The Editor named in Setup (Editor program) cannot be
 | | started.  Correct the field.
Edit / Preview / Print Document: The editor ended with status N | Edit /
 | Preview / Print Document | The Editor stopped with a status other than 0.
 | | The document may be unchanged.
Font: Only letters, digits and . _ - + = , can be used for the package,
 options, archive and map file; not saved | Font panel | One of those fields
 | | has another character.  Nothing is saved.
Font: The family is roman, sans or mono; not saved | Font panel | The field
 | | Family has another value.
Fonts: the text of a failed write | TeX Font Association | The list of fonts
 | | could not be saved: {x:appcfg-write-errors} (here in the wording of
 | | {n:msg-start-config}).
Install failed: TEXT | TeX Font Association | The installation failed;
 | | {x:msg-other-font} lists the texts.
Installed: Installed in DIR | TeX Font Association | The font is installed in
 | | DIR.
Installing font: TEXT | TeX Font Association | Install Now is running and TEXT
 | | names the step ({n:msg-other-font}).  {k:Esc} stops the download.
Setup: Settings are in effect but could not be saved | Setup | The file of
 | | settings could not be written.  They are used until the program ends.  See
 | | {x:appcfg-write-errors}.
.end
.h3 The refusals of Setup [msg-docmgr-setup]
.ix Setup, refused values
.ix Refused values, Setup
When a field of Setup holds a value that cannot be used, the reason is on the
line at the foot of the panel when the focus leaves the field, and again when
{k:Ins} is pressed; the panel stays open and nothing is saved.
.table 31 29
Text | Meaning and what to do
A word processor is not a PDF viewer | PDF Viewer names a word processor.
Backups Kept is a whole number from 0 to 99 | Backups Kept has another value.
The autosave interval is 1 to 86400 seconds | Autosave Interval (Seconds) is
 not a whole number in that range.
The Dictionary Language is a code such as en_US or de_DE | The language has a
 character that is not a letter, a digit, an underline, a minus or an at sign.
The initial working directory does not exist | Initial Working Directory is
 not a directory.
The PDF Directory is a full path or starts with ~/ | PDF Directory is a
 relative path.
The PDF viewer is not an executable file | PDF Viewer names a file that cannot
 be run.
The PDF viewer needs its full path, such as /usr/bin/evince | PDF Viewer is not
 a full path.
The PDF viewer or its directory can be changed by other users: it is not used
 | The file or its directory is writable by others, or belongs to another user.
The window rows are a whole number, or empty | Window Rows has another value.
Undo Levels is a whole number from 0 to 500 | Undo Levels has another value.
.end
.h3 Questions and the error output [msg-docmgr-more]
.ix Questions, Document Manager
.table 31 29
Text | Meaning
New File: document type (Structured, Unstructured) | Edit / Preview /
 | Print Document, new name.
.end
.table 33 27
Error output | When
<Document Manager> needs an interactive terminal (or an X display with the x11
 build) | There is no terminal and no display.
usage: <Document Manager> [document] | The first line of the usage text
 | that the option for the usage writes on the standard output.
.end
